# GitOps Conventions

This repo deploys everything through ArgoCD App-of-Apps
(`gitops/root-app.yaml` → `gitops/apps/*.yaml`). Follow these rules when
touching any manifest under `gitops/` or a component's `k8s/` directory.

## repoURL placeholder

Every ArgoCD `Application` resource must use the literal placeholder:

```yaml
repoURL: https://github.com/YOUR_ORG/agentic-doc-generation.git
```

Never replace this with a real URL in committed manifests —
`gitops/bootstrap.sh` substitutes it at bootstrap time via `sed`.

## Sync-wave ordering

Preserve `argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave` annotations:

- Wave 0 — `github-mcp-server`
- Wave 1 — `doc-gen-agent` (depends on wave 0's Service DNS name),
  `compliance-mcp-server`

Model inference on this branch goes to a configurable external
OpenAI-compatible endpoint (no in-cluster operator/CRD dependency for
inference). The `local-model` branch preserves the original three-wave
ordering (`rhoai-operator` → `model-serving`/`github-mcp-server` →
`doc-gen-agent`) for in-cluster GPU serving.

**`github-mcp-server` and `compliance-mcp-server` are deployed via an
`MCPServer` custom resource** (`k8s/mcpserver.yaml`, reconciled by RHOAI's
`mcplifecycleoperator` DataScienceCluster component into an
operator-owned Deployment/Service/NetworkPolicy), not a hand-written
Deployment — this makes them visible under OpenShift AI's AI Hub
"Deployed MCP Servers" tab. This is a deliberate exception to this
branch's "no in-cluster operator/CRD dependency" design: both now
require `./install-openshift-ai.sh` to have been run first (same
imperative-prerequisite pattern as `ci-cd-pipeline`'s Tekton CRDs — see
README) so the `MCPServer` CRD exists before ArgoCD syncs. Don't let the
operator manage a Deployment/Service with the same name as one it
doesn't already own — it refuses to adopt resources with no controller
owner (delete the old resource first; see git history for the original
hand-written Deployment+Service shape if you ever need to revert).

If you add a resource that depends on another wave's output (a CRD, a
Service DNS name, a ConfigMap), give it a sync-wave annotation at least
one higher than its dependency, don't just rely on apply order.

## Resource/namespace conventions

- All app-namespace resources (model serving, MCP server, agent) live in
  `doc-gen-demo`. Don't introduce a new namespace without a reason.
- Every container needs `resources.requests`/`limits`, a `livenessProbe`,
  and a `readinessProbe` — copy an existing `deployment.yaml` rather than
  inventing a new shape. Containers run as non-root (`USER 1001`).

## File-backed ConfigMaps

`ogx-stack-config` and `agent-knowledge` are generated from files by each
component's `build-and-deploy.sh` (`oc create configmap --from-file=...`),
not committed as inline YAML (avoids YAML-in-YAML). Follow this pattern
for new file-backed ConfigMaps, and note how it's generated in a comment
at the top of the consuming `deployment.yaml`.
